  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "The entire software increment is developed within the Spring XD project framework, building on the existing 1.2.x branch.",
    "The core technical work centers on dependency management and module configuration updates within the Spring XD build (Maven/Gradle).",
    "U1 (DLQ Enhancement): The configuration will be implemented by extending the existing sink/module options model. The additional headers (including exception/stack trace) will be added in the error handling framework component.",
    "U2 (CDC Module): A new, OOTB (Out-Of-The-Box) source module will be designed and implemented. It will use the Debezium library for database change data capture (CDC) and present events as a Spring Integration stream within XD.",
    "U3 (RabbitMQ HA): This will be implemented by enhancing the existing RabbitMQ source/sink modules to accept and properly utilize multiple broker addresses (a comma-separated list or a `host1:port1,host2:port2` format) for connection factory configuration, enabling cluster connection.",
    "U4 (Gemfire Upgrade): This involves updating the Gemfire client/server libraries in the Spring Data Gemfire dependency tree within Spring XD and validating compatibility with the new API. Changes will be confined to the Gemfire module and its tests.",
    "U5 (Colocation & Leader Election): The core change is to modify the container launch mechanism to allow multiple module instances (of the same or different streams) to run within a single Spring XD container JVM. Leader election will be implemented using a distributed lock (e.g., via Zookeeper or the existing Spring Integration distributed lock) integrated into the module deployment lifecycle.",
    "U6 & U7 (Spring Integration Upgrades): These are primarily dependency version bumps and integration testing to ensure compatibility with the new Spring Integration and SI-Kafka APIs. No major architectural changes are anticipated.",
    "U8 (Boot & Dependency Upgrades): This is a major coordinated version bump across a large list of libraries. The work is systematic: update parent POM, update individual dependency versions, resolve any resulting API changes or incompatibilities, and run the full integration test suite."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "I have deep familiarity with the Spring XD codebase, its module model, and its build system.",
    "All target dependency versions (Spring Boot 1.2.3, Spring Integration GA, Gemfire 8.1, etc.) are stable and available at the time of development.",
    "The existing test suites (unit, integration) for all affected modules are comprehensive and will serve as the primary validation tool after upgrades.",
    "No UI (Dashboard) changes are required for these user stories; all work is in backend modules, configuration, and core framework.",
    "The scope of U5 (Leader Election) is limited to a basic, functional implementation for failover between containers. A production-grade, highly sophisticated election system is out of scope for this increment.",
    "Documentation updates are not included in this effort estimate."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Build & Dependency Configuration Update",
      "activity_description": "Update the parent POM and core build configuration files (e.g., spring-xd-dirt/build.gradle) to incorporate the new versions of Spring Boot, Spring Integration, Spring Data Gemfire, and all other dependencies listed in U8. Resolve any initial build conflicts.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Core Dependency & Library Upgrades (U8, U6, U7)",
      "activity_description": "Systematically update the specified dependency versions in the build (logback, jackson, h2, tomcat, etc.) and perform integration testing across all modules to catch compilation errors, deprecated API usage, and behavioral changes. Primarily focused on Spring Boot 1.2.3 sync and Spring Integration milestone/GA release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Spring Integration Kafka Upgrade & Testing",
      "activity_description": "Specifically update the SI-Kafka dependency version, adapt any Kafka source/sink modules to API changes, and run targeted tests to verify message production and consumption.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Spring Data Gemfire Upgrade & Validation",
      "activity_name": "Update the Spring Data Gemfire and Gemfire client libraries to version 8.1. Modify Gemfire module code if necessary for API compatibility. Execute the Gemfire module's integration test suite against a local Gemfire 8.1 cluster.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U1: DLQ Enhancement Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Modify the error handling and module configuration infrastructure to support an alternative DLQ configuration option. Implement logic to capture exception details and stack traces, and add them as custom headers when publishing the message to the configured DLQ. Write unit and integration tests for the new configuration and header behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U2: Database CDC Module Development",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a new Spring XD source module named 'cdc' or similar. Integrate the Debezium engine to capture database changes (insert, update, delete) as a stream of events. Implement configuration options for database connection, table monitoring, and serialization format. Write comprehensive tests, including unit tests for the module logic and integration tests with a sample database.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U3: RabbitMQ HA Connection Support",
      "activity_description": "Update the RabbitMQ source and sink module configurations and underlying connection factory beans to accept and parse a list of broker addresses. Ensure the connection can failover between nodes in a RabbitMQ cluster. Test the connection against a multi-node RabbitMQ setup configured for HA/FT.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U5: Container Colocation & Leader Election",
      "activity_description": "Refactor the container deployment service to allow multiple stream modules to be launched and managed within a single JVM. Implement a leader election mechanism (using a distributed lock) that is checked during module startup, allowing only the leader to actively process data, with follower instances in a standby state. Implement failover triggering on leader failure. Test with multiple streams and simulated container failures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 50
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 178
  }
}
